The Vulkan backend's display and window surface for iOS (Minato's ADR-0044, decision 3; ADR-0029, decision 8).

Why: Vulkan's platform code exists for macOS only and builds only under is_mac (vulkan_backend.gni), while
Display.cpp asks for the Mac display on every Apple platform, so an iOS build with the Vulkan backend lacks
IsVulkanMacDisplayAvailable and CreateVulkanMacDisplay. DisplayVkMac imports Cocoa, and WindowSurfaceVkMac adds a
CAMetalLayer sublayer of its own, sized through autoresizingMask, which iOS lacks. This patch adds the iOS display
and window surface, made from the macOS ones: no Cocoa and no IOSurface client buffers; the window is the
CAMetalLayer the surface draws to, used as it is, as SurfaceMtl does on iOS, so that its owner keeps seeing each
drawable it presents; the current window size is the layer's bounds times its contentsScale, as MoltenVK gives a
surface's current extent, and the drawable size stays the swapchain's. They keep the Mac display's function names,
so Display.cpp's Apple branch picks the iOS display without a change.
Upstream: could go upstream, with names of their own for iOS.
Remove: when upstream builds the Vulkan backend for iOS.

